@startuml city_list_by_state
title GET /states/{stateId}/cities — List Cities of a State

actor Client
participant "CityController" as Controller
participant "ListCitiesByStateUseCase\n<<port.in>>" as UseCase
participant "ListCitiesByStateService" as Service
participant "CityRepository\n<<port.out>>" as Repo
participant "CityJpaMapper" as Mapper
participant "CityJpaRepository\n<<spring-data>>" as JpaRepo
database "MySQL" as DB

note over Client, DB
  AuthFilter ya validó el JWT y puso el principal
  en SecurityContextHolder antes de llegar al controller.
end note

note over Client, DB
  Hibernate `@SoftDelete` filtra automáticamente:
  - DELETE → UPDATE enabled=false
  - Todo SELECT añade WHERE enabled=true
end note

Client -> Controller : GET /states/{stateId}/cities
activate Controller

Controller -> UseCase : listByState(stateId)
note right of UseCase: (sin @PreAuthorize)
UseCase -> Service : listByState(stateId)
activate Service

Service -> Repo : findByStateId(stateId)
activate Repo
Repo -> JpaRepo : findAllByState_Id(stateId)
JpaRepo -> DB : SELECT city\nWHERE state_id=?\nJOIN FETCH state
DB --> JpaRepo : rows[]
JpaRepo --> Repo : List<CityJpaEntity>
Repo -> Mapper : toDomain(entity) por cada row
Mapper --> Repo : List<City>
Repo --> Service : List<City>
deactivate Repo

Service -> Service : stream().map(CityDto::from).toList()
Service --> UseCase : List<CityDto>
UseCase --> Controller : List<CityDto>
deactivate Service

Controller -> Controller : stream().map(toResponse).toList()
Controller --> Client : 200 OK\nList<CityResponse>
deactivate Controller

@enduml
